# Keep project-state.md current

`project-state.md` is the living handoff for NexusQ. After any code, design, ops, or content change in this repo, update it in the same turn before considering the work done.

## When to update

- New, changed, or removed UI, routes, components, or assets
- Architecture / stack / env / deploy changes
- Bugs fixed or newly known; backlog items added or dropped
- Merges, branch status, or production deploy notes

## What to keep accurate

- Header: last updated date, branch, latest relevant commit
- Active homepage background / current production look
- Homepage composition and key source layout
- Recent UI/UX updates (add a dated entry)
- Pending bugs, backlog, next steps, definition of done

Do not leave `project-state.md` describing a previous homepage, deleted routes, or stale next steps.

Do not expand product scope in that file beyond what was actually shipped unless Lead approved it.
